-- The v3 `required_capabilities` default is contextual ("platform lane minimum") and the pinned specification does not enumerate one universal array. The current model therefore preserves omission separately from an explicit empty array; it does not invent capabilities.
-- `backend_config.settings` is backend/version-owned. Configuration decoding requires a caller-supplied exact validator and refuses the entry when no matching registry is available.
-- Direct decode errors initially retained verbose TOML parser rendering. Before handoff, `DocumentError` was introduced so `errors.Is`/`errors.As` remain available while rendered messages expose only a static clause and cannot echo paths/endpoints/values.
-- Initial full-suite gates failed only because traceability tests still expected 30 acceptance cases after two scoped cases were added. Expectations were updated to 32; the accepted reruns are green.
-- Durable backup/fsync/atomic replacement, crash recovery, and downgrade diagnostic mutation remain owned by sibling `TASK-260830-1qf777`; this task performs no durable config mutation.
